1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,960
 If you invested $1,000 into SanDisk one year ago, you would have $34,000 today.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,920
 But you missed it, and you can't afford to miss what's coming next.

3
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:12,200
 The CEO of NVIDIA says robots are the next stage of the AI trade.

4
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:16,620
 But the money isn't in the AI, it's in the muscles and the parts that move the robot.

5
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,500
 Those are called the actuators.

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,440
 A humanoid needs over 40 actuators, and together, they cost more than half the entire robot.

7
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,440
 More than the chips, the camera, and the battery put together.

8
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,220
 So here's how I'm going to own it.

9
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:29,180
 First is Moog.

10
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:33,680
 They've made the parts that move machines for 75 years, from fighter jets to factory arms.

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
 So while everybody else is racing to figure out actuators from scratch,

12
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:40,120
 Moog has been building them since before most of these companies even existed.

13
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,700
 Their sales just hit a record.

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,060
 Second is Symbiotic.

15
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:44,760
 They're not promising new humanoids.

16
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:48,700
 They build the robots that are already existing inside of the Walmart warehouses of today.

17
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:52,740
 That matters because almost everything in the space is a demo video or a promise.

18
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,440
 And this is a company that's already getting paid for it.

19
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:58,480
 They've got $22 billion of orders signed and waiting.

20
00:00:58,980 --> 00:00:59,880
 Third is COID.

21
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:03,440
 It's a basket that holds the whole robot's supply chain in one ticker.

22
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,000
 Nobody actually knows which of these companies wins.

23
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,940
 So this is a version where you don't have to guess.

24
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,360
 And fourth is the layer underneath everything, MP materials.

25
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:15,500
 Every single one of those actuators needs a magnet to work.

26
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,900
 And a robot uses two to three more times magnets than an electric car.

27
